00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:08.380
Speaker 1: Russia is now threatening American
assets in response to the first round of sanctions

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.240
to the first round of sanctions.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.849
Let's start there.

00:00:12.849 --> 00:00:14.860
Business Insider reporting.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:20.640
Russia threatens to target sensitive U.S.
assets as part of a strong and painful response

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:26.730
to U.S.. Sanctions, its Foreign Ministry of
Foreign Affairs Ministry said the sanctions

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:30.000
were attempt to change Russia's course.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.660
There should be no doubt that sanctions will
receive a strong response.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:42.410
Russia's Foreign Affairs Ministry said the
country would target sensitive American assets

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.039
in retaliation.

00:00:44.039 --> 00:00:47.180
The ministry said this is part of America's.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:51.970
The sanctions are part of America's ongoing
attempts to change Russia's course.

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:57.859
Russia has proved that despite all the sanctions
cost, it is able to minimize the damage and

00:00:57.859 --> 00:01:04.190
even more so, sanctions pressure is not able
to effect our determination to firmly defend

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:06.370
our interests, it added.

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:11.090
There should be no doubt that sanctions will
receive a strong response not necessarily

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:16.750
symmetrical, but finely tuned and painful
to the American side.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:21.470
The United States, on the other hand, plans
to continue escalating the sanctions.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:28.890
I don't even pretend to know where this will
end, but it is very clear that all along,

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:34.020
you know, we had we had reports which said,
here's what we know.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.160
Here's what could happen.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:39.390
And then here's a less bad scenario.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:45.700
Just about every element of this so far has
been closer to the worst case scenario.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.880
Now, obviously, there were people talking
about nuclear war as a worst case scenario.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.480
I don't believe that will happen.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:54.240
I don't believe we're going in that direction.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:02:00.010
I think that that that's that's quite literally
it would be a suicide decision by Putin and

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.010
Russia.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:04.800
But from from the sort of more reasonable,
could this be trying to take a little bit

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:05.800
of territory?

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.880
Could this escalate into bombing Kiev?

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.400
It's all going in the worst direction.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:16.900
And economically, it's also already doing
significant, significant damage.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:20.530
Understand also, by the way, that.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:24.560
Russia has changed its tune on the sanctions
pretty quickly, I mean, just two days ago,

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:29.299
Russia was saying, we don't care about sanctions,
they're not really going to do anything.

00:02:29.299 --> 00:02:35.879
Now Russia is saying the sanctions are painful
and we are going to retaliate specifically

00:02:35.879 --> 00:02:36.959
for the sanctions.

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:42.230
So it should not be lost on us that Russia
has changed its opinion of the sanctions,

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:43.230
